2. In the code-behind, we define a recursive method `DrawSierpinskiTriangleRecursive` to draw the Sierpinski triangle.
3. The `DrawSierpinskiTriangle` method is called when the control is loaded and when the size changes.
4. The `DrawTriangle` method draws a single triangle.
5. In the `MainWindow.xaml`, we use the `SierpinskiTriangle` control.

To change the number of iterations, you can set the `Iterations` property of the `SierpinskiTriangle` control.

