Once inside the Nix shell, you should have access to LLVM 17 tools like `clang-17`, `llvm-config`, etc.

### 2. Directly Using `nix-shell` Command

If you don't want to create a `shell.nix` file, you can directly use the `nix-shell` command with the `-p` option to specify the packages you want to be available in the shell.

Here's how you can do it:

```sh
nix-shell -p llvm_17
```

This command will drop you into a Nix shell with LLVM 17 available.

### Considerations

- Make sure your Nixpkgs is up to date. You can update Nixpkgs by running `nix-channel --update nixpkgs` (assuming you're using the `nixpkgs` channel).
